      "content": "Thanks for the draft. It's a bit too brief, honestly. The techs might miss something important if it's just one paragraph. \n\nCan you expand this into a more comprehensive manual? Break it down into more detailed steps like \"Installation,\" \"Wiring,\" \"Software Configuration,\" and \"Troubleshooting.\" \n\nAlso, like I said before, the QC tool is what gets this approved by the system, and a score of 8 is pretty low for a technical document. Try to get that complexity score up—maybe use more sub-headings or more detailed bulleted lists for the different phases—but again, please keep it professional. I don't want a disorganized mess, just a more thorough, well-structured guide.",
