      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is the **Nexus-7 Optical Sensor Field Installation Guide**, structured to ensure technician safety and comprehensive procedural coverage.\n\n# **Nexus-7 Optical Sensor: Field Installation & Operation Manual**\n\n## **1. Safety & Prerequisites**\nBefore beginning, ensure the technician has the correct tools and understands critical safety limits to prevent equipment damage.\n\n### **1.1 Environmental Precautions**\n*   Never expose the sensor to direct sunlight; this causes calibration drift and potential pupil overheating.\n*   Work in a dry environment with a relative humidity below 60% to prevent connector corrosion.\n*   Use a static-dissipative wrist strap during assembly to protect sensitive glass optics from electrostatic discharge.\n\n### **1.2 Mandatory Safety Checks**\n*   The voltage supply must be strictly regulated at 5V DC; input voltages exceeding 5V can permanently burn the internal circuit board.\n*   Verify that the M3 screw holes are clean of debris before applying torque to avoid warping the aluminum housing.\n*   Ensure the data cable is untangled and routed to prevent strain on the brittle ribbons inside the connector.\n\n## **2. Hardware Installation**\nThis section",
